nts","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":5800443,"digest":"sha256:757c720e02e639c7342d1f01bf6c6ef619ea7c83b67890f3320f8ff16e02bb29","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T19:44:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:44:29Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/chester-hill-solutions/stow-s3/releases/download/v0.3.0/stow-linux-amd64.tar.gz"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chester-hill-solutions/stow-s3/releases/assets/641458941","id":641458941,"node_id":"RA_kwDOTYnIys4mO-L9","name":"stow-linux-arm64.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":5233382,"digest":"sha256:5c344c5a8f48ac754a46564684621cc2fe299f6ab567595f72cbaec08df23c44","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T19:44:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:44:29Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/chester-hill-solutions/stow-s3/releases/download/v0.3.0/stow-linux-arm64.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chester-hill-solutions/stow-s3/tarball/v0.3.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chester-hill-solutions/stow-s3/zipball/v0.3.0","body":"# Stow v0.3.0\n\nS3-shaped storage for development, agents and controlled private deployments,\nwith native filesystem storage and a browser WASM runtime.\n\n## Distribution\n\nThis release provides native downloads on GitHub for Linux and macOS, on x86_64\nand ARM64. Each archive contains `stow-s3`, the license and the README.\nVerify the downloaded archive against `SHA256SUMS.txt` from the same release.\n\nnpm and PyPI publication are deferred. TypeScript and Python clients remain\navailable from source; this release does not claim registry installation works.\nExecuted live AWS S3, Cloudflare R2 and custom-provider receipts are not part of\nthis downloads-only release. The local conformance and artifact-consumer gates\nstill run before publication.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Native workspaces support preparation, immutable checkpoints, portable handoff,\n  adoption, guarded saves and recovery of interrupted save requests.\n- Browser storage supports file history, atomic project revisions, IndexedDB\n  persistence, workers and bounded object streams through the binary WASM bridge.\n- Filesystem objects use protobuf metadata and raw payloads. Header-only listing,\n  incremental managed usage accounting and streaming reads avoid full-payload\n  decoding during metadata and quota operations.\n- Ordinary unbound filesystem uploads stage outside the runtime publication lock;\n  uploads and copies use bounded payload scratch while retaining atomic publication.\n- Independent reads overlap safely and return caller-owned bytes. Internally owned\n  HTTP bodies avoid redundant copying without changing caller ownership rules.\n- The embedded implementation is isolated behind the existing public Go facade,\n  reducing the packaged WASM runtime. Browser hosts use streaming instantiation\n  where supported, and reuse stream buffers after copying bytes into JavaScript.\n- Native workspace indexes use compact encoding, with unchanged fields and format\n  version. Each index update still replaces the complete index.\n\n## Filesystem upgrade compatibility\n\nExisting version-1 JSON object records remain readable. Opening a directory does\nnot rewrite its objects. New or overwritten objects use version-2 records with\nprotobuf metadata and raw payloads; mixed directories are supported.\n\n**Older Stow versions cannot read version-2 records.** Preserve a backup before\nupgrading persistent object-record directories if you need a downgrade path.\nThis change applies to object-record storage, not the editable workspace layout.\nThe S3 HTTP protocol and journal JSON formats are unchanged.\n\nGuarded and capacity-bound writes retain their existing admission and recovery\npaths. Windows retains its existing captured-payload materialization; native\nworkspace support remains limited to Linux and macOS.\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload the matching `stow-linux-amd64.tar.gz`, `stow-linux-arm64.tar.gz`,\n`stow-darwin-amd64.tar.gz` or `stow-darwin-arm64.tar.gz` from this release.\nExtract it, put `stow-s3` on your PATH and check `stow-s3 --version`.\n\n```sh\nstow-s3 serve --port 0 --backend filesystem --data-dir .stow\n```\n\nRead the `STOW_READY` record for the endpoint and generated credentials, then\nconnect with an S3 SDK using path-style addressing and region `us-east-1`.\n"}